Bar applied
-----------
A small mark at a nose, an open ear line, an outlined eyebrow band, small dark
shading inside ears, or a simplified branch or bush is not a defect.
A defect is only what a teacher or a child sees at book size: a wrong or changed
character, a broken face, a clearly wrong hand or limb, a wrong or missing prop
the sentence needs, a layout fault, text in the picture, gray or shading in the
line art, or a line gap that makes coloring hard.
For an input sheet I also check: plain white background, no people, no text or
letters, the object count and parts are right, and the object reads as the word
at book size.

