park set (m2): empty sunny park. One large low tree at the left with a wide
crown and one low thick branch to the right. One pond with gray and tan stones
and lily pads at the right. One sun, two clouds, bushes at the back, open grass
in the middle foreground. No people, no animals, no text.
Builder flaw: the leaf cluster on the low branch is an odd arc shape.
Judged under the bar: a simplified branch or bush is not a defect. At book size
the cluster reads as leaves. Not a defect.
Page risk: low, not blocking. The birds page needs four birds on the branch.
The branch stays long and mostly bare, so four birds fit. That page also passes
the low-branch reference out/storytime-low-branch/views/three-quarter.png.
Pages: cover-how-many, balls-five, birds-four, cakes-seven, cakes-oh-no-pip,
